section.appendix(data-visibility="uncounted" data-hide-nav id="figure-8-5")
    p.appendix-title #[b Figure 8.5] Results of the non-superiority test for the Control Group ratings.
    .appendix-content(style="--columns: 1; --rows: 1")
        img(src="appendix/figure-8.5-0.png")
    aside.notes
        | <p>Results of the non-superiority test for the Control Group ratings. The plot displays the relative longitudinal shift (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">Test</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">Control</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{Test}} - \Delta_{\text{Control}}</annotation></semantics></math>) across the three criteria. The red dashed line denotes the perceptual noise margin (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\delta</annotation></semantics></math>) established from the baseline variability. Black dots represent the mean relative shift, and the error bars indicate the upper bound of the one-sided 95% confidence interval. The shaded region represents the zone of statistical non-superiority (rejection of <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_0</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>

section.appendix(data-visibility="uncounted" data-hide-nav id="figure-8-6")
    p.appendix-title #[b Figure 8.6] Results of the pairwise listening test on pairs recorded by a Control Violinist.
    .appendix-content(style="--columns: 1; --rows: 1")
        img(src="appendix/figure-8.6-0.png")
    aside.notes
        | <p>Results of the pairwise listening test on pairs recorded by a Control Violinist. The top three rows display the mean dissimilarity ratings (0=Identical, 10=Very Different) for <em>same-violin</em> pairs. Black markers (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">BB</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{BB}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">Before vs. Before</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{Before vs. Before}}</annotation></semantics></math>) represent the baseline dissimilarity between the two pre-intervention sessions (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1w}</annotation></semantics></math>). Grey markers (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">AB</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{AB}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">After vs. Before</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{After vs. Before}}</annotation></semantics></math>) represent the dissimilarity between an After phase take and a Before phase take. The bottom row displays the perceptual shift (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">AB</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext mathvariant="normal">BB</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{AB}} - \Delta_{\text{BB}}</annotation></semantics></math>), quantifying the audible change over 6 months after subtracting the baseline variability. Dots represent the mean rating across listeners, while the error bars represent the mean <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mi>±</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> 95% confidence interval.</p>

