section.appendix(data-visibility="uncounted" data-hide-nav id="table-9-1")
    p.appendix-title #[b Table 9.1] Repeated-measures ANOVA: visual phase
    .appendix-content(style="--columns: 1; --rows: 1")
        img(src="appendix/table-9.1.svg")
    aside.notes
        | <p>Repeated-measures ANOVA for the visual phase (Sessions 1 and 2; <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N = 11</annotation></semantics></math>). Each effect is tested as <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathit{df}_1, \mathit{df}_2)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{df}_1</annotation></semantics></math> the numerator (effect) and <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{df}_2</annotation></semantics></math> the denominator (error) degrees of freedom. Significant effects (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p &lt; 0.05</annotation></semantics></math>) are shown in bold.</p>

section.appendix(data-visibility="uncounted" data-hide-nav id="table-9-2")
    p.appendix-title #[b Table 9.2] Repeated-measures ANOVA: prestige phase
    .appendix-content(style="--columns: 1; --rows: 1")
        img(src="appendix/table-9.2.svg")
    aside.notes
        | <p>Repeated-measures ANOVA for the prestige phase (Session 3; <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N = 11</annotation></semantics></math>). Each effect is tested as <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false" form="prefix">(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false" form="postfix">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathit{df}_1, \mathit{df}_2)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{df}_1</annotation></semantics></math> the numerator (effect) and <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑑</mi><mi mathvariant="italic">𝑓</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{df}_2</annotation></semantics></math> the denominator (error) degrees of freedom. Significant effects (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p &lt; 0.05</annotation></semantics></math>) are shown in bold.</p>

section.appendix(data-visibility="uncounted" data-hide-nav id="figure-9-1")
    p.appendix-title #[b Figure 9.1] Non-blind minus blind rating differences
    .appendix-content(style="--columns: 1; --rows: 1")
        img(src="appendix/figure-9.1-0.svg")
    aside.notes
        | <p>Per-violin rating difference between the non-blind and blind conditions (<math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant="normal">non-blind</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext mathvariant="normal">blind</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta = \text{non-blind} - \text{blind}</annotation></semantics></math>), for the visual phase (left, Sessions 1 and 2) and the prestige phase (right, Session 3). Faint dots are individual players; the solid marker is the mean and the bar its <math display="inline" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> confidence interval. A positive value indicates that seeing (or knowing about) the instrument raised its rating. All four intervals include zero.</p>
